  "title": "Edge-antipodal colorings of cubes",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "We let $Q_d$ denote the $d$-dimensional cube graph. A map $\\phi: E(Q_d) \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ is called edge-antipodal if $\\phi(e) \\neq \\phi(e')$ whenever $e,e'$ are antipodal edges.\n\nConjecture If $d \\ge 2$ and $\\phi: E(Q_d) \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ is edge-antipodal, then there exist a pair of antipodal vertices $v,v' \\in V(Q_d)$ which are joined by a monochromatic path.",
